# Line-ending policy.
#
# Everything is stored LF in the repository; the working-tree ending is then
# pinned per file type below rather than left to each participant's
# core.autocrlf. Participants clone this repo onto Windows, macOS, and WSL, and
# the shell scripts here are executed by whichever bash is on PATH -- so the
# ending has to be decided by the repo, not by local config.
* text=auto

# Scripts run by bash MUST be LF. Git Bash (MSYS2) happens to strip CR, which
# masks the problem on a default Windows setup, but GNU bash under WSL and on
# macOS/Linux does not: a CRLF script fails on `fi\r` / `then\r`, taking every
# .claude/hooks/* launcher (and `./mvnw`) down with it.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which genuinely needs CRLF -- LF breaks
# multi-line constructs such as labels and goto targets.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Don't let Git rewrite bytes inside archives or images.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
